    "body": "@bzbarsky in particular this means that if the target is a binary, Firefox will download it anyways (just ignoring the suggested filename).\r\n\r\nImplementation-wise, this behavior is difficult for us to match, as Blink has to decide when the user clicks on the link whether to go down the navigation path or the download path. Reversing that decision once the URL is redirected cross origin is kinda involved.\r\n\r\nWould Firefox be willing to change its behavior to always go down the download path and abort the download if its cross origin instead?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
