    "created_at": "2017-05-16T09:07:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-16T09:07:37Z",
    "body": "That doesn't match my tests. If the URL is same origin but then redirects cross origin, Firefox still goes down the navigation route.\r\n\r\nAlso, you could argue that if the target is a binary, it should still abort the download.",
