    "created_at": "2017-05-16T12:04:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-16T12:04:15Z",
    "body": "The actual implementation in Firefox basically always goes down the navigation route, but sets a flag that says \"treat this response as if it had Content-Disposition:attachment\".  I'm pretty sure (but haven't tested) that if you have a same-origin load that redirects to same-origin that means we'll end up navigating to it, not downloading it...\r\n\r\nThis was an expedient way to implement things for the common case people really cared about (blob urls and the like) but doesn't really match the spec in any way, I agree.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
